		</nav>

		<section class="im-content im-content-flush" style="--im-content-main: 100%">
			<h2>What this lesson covers</h2>
			<p>Why a component should never name a colour, only what the colour is <em>for</em> — and why that one rule is the whole of dark mode.</p>
			<pre><code class="language-css">/* Not this */
.card { background: #f5f5f5; }

/* This */
.card { background: var(--im-surface); }</code></pre>
			<p>Two declarations, one file, and every component in the theme follows without being told.</p>
			<h3>Exercise</h3>
			<p>Take the three components you wrote in lesson 2 and remove every literal colour from them. Nothing should break in light mode; dark mode should start working on its own.</p>
			<div class="kg-card kg-callout-card kg-callout-card-blue"><div class="kg-callout-emoji">📎</div><div class="kg-callout-text">The exercise files are the same theme at the start and the end of this lesson, so you can diff them if you get stuck.</div></div>
		</section>

