<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>The player layout</h2>
		<p><code>im-course</code> is a two-column layout that changes what it <em>is</em> at <code>lg</code>, rather than only how it looks:</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Width</th><th>The curriculum</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><strong>≥ 64rem</strong></td><td>A sticky column beside the lesson, scrolling on its own. The "Curriculum" button is hidden, because the thing it opens is already open.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><strong>&lt; 64rem</strong></td><td>A panel fixed to the right edge, opened by that button — the browser's own <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>, so focus, Esc and the backdrop come free.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>
		<p>One markup, two behaviours, and the lesson keeps the whole width on a laptop where the video actually needs it.</p>

		<h2>One next thing</h2>
		<p>A lesson page has exactly one job after the video ends: get the student to the next lesson. So there is <strong>one</strong> prominent way forward — the <code>im-postnav</code> pair — and everything else on the page is quiet. No related courses, no newsletter, no footer full of links; a student who leaves here does not come back to lesson four.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>"Mark complete" is a real button</strong>, not something that happens at 90% watched. Some people read the transcript.</li>
			<li><strong>The exercise files are next to the lesson</strong>, not on a downloads page.</li>
			<li><strong>Questions belong on the lesson</strong>, not in a forum somewhere else: the answer to "why does this not work" is almost always specific to one lesson, and the next student has the same question.</li>
			<li><strong>Locked lessons stay readable.</strong> A padlock and the title — not a blur, not a removal. It is the argument for upgrading.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
